  "reason": "The current best is config_019 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) at 0.639 acc. Evidence strongly supports avgpool > transformer, weighted > concat, multiprofile > singleprofile, and multimodal > RNA-only. The one untested dimension in this best setup is the RNA encoder: we've confirmed pca_n2000 > scgpt (0.591 vs 0.530 in RNA-only), but scvi_n200 has never been tested. Config_031 makes a single-variable change (pca_n2000 → scvi_n200) from the current best, directly testing whether a different learned RNA representation could push accuracy above 0.639. This is the highest-value experiment because it isolates the RNA encoder effect in the already-optimized multimodal pipeline, and with only one experiment remaining after this, confirming or ruling out scvi_n200 in the best configuration is the most informative use of the budget."
}

